{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue went from essentially nil in FY2019 [F1] to $5,387 million in FY2025 [F7], a 48.1% three-year CAGR from FY2022 [D342]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The step change was FY2022, when revenue jumped 2914.5% to $1,658 million [D83][F4] on deliveries of 19,412 vehicles [P67], then grew 167.4% in FY2023 [D135]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Growth then decelerated sharply to 12.1% in FY2024 [D187] and 8.4% in FY2025 [D239]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The loss narrowed every year after FY2022: operating loss fell from $6,856 million [F23] to $3,585 million [F26], lifting operating margin from -413.5% [F28] to -66.5% [F31]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 Software and Services contributed +21.6pp of the 8.4% revenue growth [D295][D239], while New electric vehicles subtracted 10.5pp [D288]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Software and services revenue rose 221.7% to $1,557 million [D294][S14], primarily on vehicle electrical architecture and software development services for the Joint Venture, remarketing and repair and maintenance [P18]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "That segment reached 28.9% of revenue [D321], while Automotive fell 14.6% [D315] to 71.1% of revenue [D314]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Automotive revenue fell as deliveries dropped 9,332 vehicles, partly from expiration of 45W tax credits after September 30, 2025 [P22]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 6.9% against 8.4% revenue growth [D258][D239], an incremental operating margin of 264.7% [D265]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin turned positive at 2.7% in FY2025 [F19], against a window median of -45.8% [D332] and a FY2021 low of -845.5% [D330]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of -66.5% [F31] remains far below the -129.4% window median [D326] in absolute terms but is the window high [D325]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 bridge was almost entirely cost of revenue, +26.8pp [D267], with R&D +1.5pp [D268] and SG&A -0.5pp [D269]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Cost of revenue fell 15.0% [D255] as Automotive cost of revenues dropped on fewer vehicles produced and lower raw material, component and conversion costs [P21]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "SG&A rose 9.9% [D257] on expanding go-to-market operations, higher payroll and stock-based compensation [P13]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow was -$779 million in FY2025 [F64], a -14.5% margin [D227], against a -132.9% window median free-cash-flow margin [D335]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The improvement in operating cash use was primarily driven by a significant reduction in net loss [P4]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow was -$2,489 million [F78], a -46.2% margin [D226], with capex of $1,710 million [F71] at 31.7% of revenue [D225] and 2.18x D&A [D228]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Capex rose 49.9% [D246] on expansion of production capacity at the Normal Factory and next-generation platforms [P3]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash fell to $1,642 million in FY2025 [D231] from $3,259 million [D179], as cash and investments dropped 21.0% [D261]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash is still 30.5% of revenue [D232], above the 17.8% autos peer median (n=4) [D352] at the 75th percentile [D351]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Financing inflow of $886 million [F92] came primarily from $750 million of Class A shares issued to Volkswagen Group on the Financial Milestone [P2]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted shares rose 17.1% [D260] to 1,186 million [X91], so EPS improved 34.5% [D242] while net loss fell 23.2% [D241]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net losses persist in all seven years, from -$426 million in FY2019 [F32] to -$3,646 million in FY2025 [F38] [R1]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Stock-based compensation was 13.8% of revenue in FY2025 [D223] and at least 10% in each of the last five years [R2], equal to 20.7% of the operating loss [D237]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cash and investments of $6,082 million [D229] cover 2.4 years of the latest burn [D236] [R3]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "New electric vehicles were 67.6% of revenue [D286] and fell 12.5% [D287] [R4], and Automotive fell 14.6% [D315] [R5]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Product revenue members sum to 129% of consolidated revenue in FY2025, so they cannot be added [R6]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin: a move above the FY2025 level of 2.7% [F19] would confirm the cost trend; a slip back below zero would reverse it, visible in the FY2026 10-K."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin: holding above the -66.5% window high [D325] confirms the narrowing loss; falling back toward the -129.4% median [D326] would reverse it."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash: staying above the FY2025 $1,642 million [D231] confirms the balance sheet holds; a drop below the 2.4 years of burn coverage [D236] would tighten liquidity."}
  ]}
]}
